            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I does indeed make sense to test different kinds of behavior, but I think it is better to do in a single test.\n\nPrepare with three new global and one new local sessions (all should set appropriate `_G.session_file` variable):\n- `session_cd_global` - changes directory to 'dir-sessions/global'.\n- `session_cd_local` - changes directory to 'dir-sessions/local'.\n- `session_cd_local-2` - changes directory to 'dir-sessions/local-2'.\n- `Session.vim` inside new 'dir-sessions/local-2'.\n\nThe test `makes detected local session up to date` then:\n- Starts in 'dir-sessions/local' with `Session.vim` detected.\n- Reads `session_cd_global` and then `detected` should not contain `Session.vim`. Tests `yes session -> no session`.\n- Reads `session_cd_local` and then `detected` should contain `Session.vim`. Tests `no session -> yes session`.\n- Reads `session_cd_local-2` and then `detected` should contain another `Session.vim`. Tests `yes session -> yes another session`.\n\nThis doesn't cover `no session -> no session`, but I think it is fine.",
            "commit_id": "d1050081a75aee5900bfca58a0de72ae528d3f03",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-02-13T20:38:23Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -358,6 +358,51 @@ T['read()']['makes detected sessions up to date'] = function()\n   validate_session_loaded('global/new_session')\n end\n \n+T['read()']['removes stale local session from detected'] = function()",
